"""
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
This is the Manana template language. Manana is a whitespace-semantic
language for HTML & XML that implements "Views", allowing the user to break up
their markup into a tree of first-class objects.

A few rules about Manana:

1. Every View converts to, and acts as, a pure function (no side effects)
2. Since every view is a function, a View can accept input arguments
3. Indentation delimits blocks and auto-generates closing tags
4. The "@" symbol denotes a "directive" to the Manana engine
5. The ">" symbol acts as an "inline indentation", allowing tags to be chained
   in a single line of code.
6. Attributes follow the pattern: `(k=v k=v ...)` and can span multiple lines
7. Inside an "attribute map", whitespace means nothing and values that don't
   have spaces can be left unquoted.
7. "a" tags have a special syntax using the "/[...]" for syntactic sugar
   instead of having to type '(href="/some-url")'
8. At any point in Manana code, you can create block comments with the
   triple-double-quotes syntax that surrounds this very text.
9. Any line that starts with a letter, and matches an HTML5 tag, will be
   treated as one
10. Code blocks are declared using "```...```"
11. Code blocks calculate starting indentation based on the number of
    whitespace tokens before the first character in the first line. All code
    after that uses that as zero-indent, as if it were pushed all the way
    up against the left side of the file with zero spaces.
12. Manana implements "parse modes" that tell the parser which mode it is in.
13. "parse modes" include:
    - "std" for standard mode
    - "attr" for inside attribute maps
    - "code" for code blocks
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
"""

@manana 0.1

@view _main
div#page.container.width-full
  @left-nav
  @page-content
  @sidebar
  @other-view-1 ^:manana/allow-missing
  @other-view-2 ^:manana/allow-missing
    @other-view-3
  @other-view-4 ^:manana/allow-missing
    @other-view-5

@view left-nav
ul
  li > a /                Home
  li > a /about           About Us
  li > a (/contact)       Contact
  li > a (
    href = "/syntax"
  ) This is valid in Manana

@view page-content
div#content.conttainer.h-full
  h1 Welcome to Manana!

  p.row
    h2 Very nested syntax:
    ul#some-id.a.b.c > li(*x 1) > a /link Link Text

  p.row
    h2 Variable interpolation
    P.p-2
      Here's some text in the Manana template language
      that includes {user.first-name} {user.last-name}
      and here's how you literally print those braces:
      \{user.first-name} \{user.last-name}.

  p.row
    h2 Some code that converts to <pre><code>...</code></pre>

    ```
    if (x === undefined) {
      console.log("x is undefined");
    }
    ```

@view sidebar
  li > a /link1 Link 1
  li > a /link2 Link 2
  li > a /link3 Link 3
